#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7a0aba38-1167-5365-bbd2-cd2ba7e57b15" :question/math-academy-id "e-612" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\langle 6t^5+2t, \\sec^2 t\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨6{t}^{5}+2t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (6{t}^{5}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7a39ddf2-3ba2-534f-8dca-93497cae823f" :question/math-academy-id "e-613" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left\\langle\\cos(2t+1), \\, 4\\right\\rangle \\,\\textrm d t\\,.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t) =\\cos(2t+1),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u= 2t +1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d t} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d t = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) =4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int 4\\text{d}t=4t+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,4t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6da4ce70-1718-53bb-8831-a93fdc3e4677" :question/math-academy-id "e-614" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩. \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{t}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨[2{e}^{2}-2{e}^{0}],\\,[2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}-2,\\,16⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/id #uuid "76a0fefe-71fd-5500-a4d8-7d5f8a09613e" :question/math-academy-id "e-615" :question/problem "Calculate $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t, \\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf F(0)=\\langle 0,\\, 0\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t,\\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $\\mathbf F(0)=\\left\\langle 0,\\, 0 \\right\\rangle$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡0+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $c_1=-1$ and $c_2=\\dfrac 12.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\left\\langle  \\sec t - 1  , \\,  -\\dfrac 1 2\\cos(2t)+ \\dfrac12\\right\\rangle.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9718da6a-a6d4-578f-a9c3-2f206c80893d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297271} {:answer/id #uuid "5ebd9470-2213-5605-aa8b-ecd8429f99b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297272} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6de13a-1cff-5322-a826-c0d7072def1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297273} {:answer/id #uuid "abddcc28-4e8f-52e1-97ec-9cbdf72a424f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297274} {:answer/id #uuid "82637355-748d-5358-ab04-687b5c68f99b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82637355-748d-5358-ab04-687b5c68f99b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297275} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f62d617-6d02-5db0-9f4e-3940f13ae4fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52390093-006a-5954-b55c-8b4eeb61a32f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123224" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57f86693-d0c9-5197-a2fa-6957664c987c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332916} {:answer/id #uuid "879ffb98-166e-5021-af99-d6f669ca6e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332917} {:answer/id #uuid "89d996e9-9acc-574a-bbef-ad333b8a2306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332918} {:answer/id #uuid "93c0cbab-c639-5c24-ba08-925b751df106" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332919} {:answer/id #uuid "f3aa2883-0b9d-5fb5-ba7d-c8f4d81885ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t),\\,{sin}^{2}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89d996e9-9acc-574a-bbef-ad333b8a2306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332918} :answer-field/id #uuid "308e1365-bc5a-5995-8534-adfad73ed0d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83aa510b-e988-5498-be95-547a695eb498" :question/math-academy-id "q-123320" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101cbc3d-8ada-5787-9d21-feee751379e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332923} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce5478b-9a72-55ff-b65d-51d747a90918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t-1},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332924} {:answer/id #uuid "eb066872-e293-5a52-8a19-b26ef182a5a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332925} {:answer/id #uuid "c3220efa-582f-58e2-a10e-77732718dde1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t-1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332926} {:answer/id #uuid "97612383-f607-5ead-84a2-f7aff88224f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{5t},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "101cbc3d-8ada-5787-9d21-feee751379e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332923} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a90f7e6-ebbb-53f5-b993-94997e7d0347" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f7f0bed-7a5e-5c15-8327-bc7f4c63ab8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123437" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)={e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\text{d}t={e}^{t}+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52ce1447-b0e5-5f2a-987c-362f6d0d46e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,3t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332930} {:answer/id #uuid "2e215379-4040-5a8f-800c-e5c6db1212b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332931} {:answer/id #uuid "1bcee2ac-675c-5f32-ab97-d9bf176c87c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332932} {:answer/id #uuid "19717bac-4237-5d76-a720-c8dcbf7eda29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,2t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332933} {:answer/id #uuid "42108951-81c9-56b3-8980-0c115e0adb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,6t{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e215379-4040-5a8f-800c-e5c6db1212b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332931} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6fe81d9-832d-50de-b858-d79aa164d2fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4f8fc37-cca0-530f-8347-2eb6c354f4a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-123450" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,6t{e}^{({t}^{2}-1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,6t{e}^{({t}^{2}-1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 6t{e}^{({t}^{2}-1)}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=6t{e}^{({t}^{2}-1)},$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u={t}^{2}-1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2t\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2t}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 6t{e}^{({t}^{2}-1)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 6t{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2t}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{e}^{u}+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =3{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,6t{e}^{({t}^{2}-1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,3{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{{t}^{2}-1}⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea3c7f4a-c072-5c21-b514-7491b0307349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332937} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fbc396-687c-5932-ae5e-517e58a209ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\sqrt{2}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332938} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8aeac5-0608-55fa-86ba-2fd15f406f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2-\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332939} {:answer/id #uuid "d61b0d03-74f7-5115-aec6-5d0be34eb5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332940} {:answer/id #uuid "0b0d661a-8de7-5b4e-b8af-63ab8f467f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{2},\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8fbc396-687c-5932-ae5e-517e58a209ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\sqrt{2}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332938} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6df3ca9-9779-51b2-b842-2959e2fbeaab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb8b3222-c045-5fd0-b252-08063208b15e" :question/math-academy-id "q-123455" :question/problem "${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}⟨\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t},\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}⟨\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t},\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1,\\,\\sqrt{2}-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\sqrt{2}-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3914a990-f10b-5eab-a43b-a38059132bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332944} {:answer/id #uuid "b7216938-c3eb-57b3-8f84-a17622cdf910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332945} {:answer/id #uuid "0023e485-9f1d-5dd6-a4d8-9439dbc86f4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})-2,\\,t+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332946} {:answer/id #uuid "98db7085-865f-526b-ae26-8094e5080586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})-1,\\,{t}^{2}+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332947} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4fa49a-5431-5531-9294-268e54d3ef02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc4fa49a-5431-5531-9294-268e54d3ef02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332948} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a4fc821-29c8-5a74-8daf-915001f4cadc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f39c4f8-ac41-5b15-bc05-f02a4b75d093" :question/math-academy-id "q-123470" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,3⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{2}{t},\\,2t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{2}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 2t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,3⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})+{c}_{1},\\,(1)^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=2.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})+1,\\,{t}^{2}+2⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2d23ef0-0b7f-5141-be91-ee6cc6610eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332951} {:answer/id #uuid "b94ab33f-1a30-5aaf-817c-3eba7b1831d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332952} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a5b411-336e-51fe-8ab3-55e2088c195f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332953} {:answer/id #uuid "90eaad86-4441-535a-a919-a0fa4bcd1ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{sec}^{2}⁡t-3,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332954} {:answer/id #uuid "ab95f828-5fd5-5c17-bf84-e9a6ce37bf3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2d23ef0-0b7f-5141-be91-ee6cc6610eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332951} :answer-field/id #uuid "73928db4-1843-53d5-aae7-df1684f68398" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff7e196f-5947-5cda-8ba7-68642d1d79ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-123472" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩$ and $F(\\pi )=⟨-3,\\,3⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(\\pi )=⟨-3,\\,3⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\pi )=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi )+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨-3,\\,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨-1+{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨-3,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-2$ and ${c}_{2}=3.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-2,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+3⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b897f139-a4ba-5344-8a98-287f18f06309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{3}-5,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332958} {:answer/id #uuid "cbfb4e63-de6c-5a4b-9499-09e4228e5459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{4}-4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332959} {:answer/id #uuid "130ced5e-2101-50d3-a5cf-0ba1213c922a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{4}+4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332960} {:answer/id #uuid "fa75420d-2c57-58b9-a218-e4b4de77f891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{5}-4,\\,4{(t-1)}^{2}+5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332961} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6d4f96-cf20-5241-910f-416af48283de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2}-4,\\,4{({t}^{4}-1)}^{2}-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbfb4e63-de6c-5a4b-9499-09e4228e5459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5{t}^{4}-4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332959} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf022d1-f4cf-53df-be49-568ea2c868a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbc5ca63-1df5-5c8f-890f-d266498c8163" :question/math-academy-id "q-123473" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨20{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,5⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨20{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨20{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 20{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 16t({t}^{2}-1)\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5{t}^{4}+{c}_{1},\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,5⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨5\\cdot {1}^{4}+{c}_{1},\\,4{({1}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,5⟩ \\\\ ⟨5+{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-4$ and ${c}_{2}=5.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨5{t}^{4}-4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4445b6b7-0280-50d9-ab9d-cc1c2e794140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,5{e}^{5t}-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332965} {:answer/id #uuid "7b77aede-9c55-5ec3-9e49-8d826f858596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}-2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332966} {:answer/id #uuid "cac5345a-435b-5d99-86cd-ad99e17a19b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332967} {:answer/id #uuid "34364ab1-eb6b-513e-b87a-98bf44363d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{1/3}+1,\\,{e}^{t}-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332968} {:answer/id #uuid "f05d4e77-3f85-5d2a-b440-3d79f4567766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{2t}-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cac5345a-435b-5d99-86cd-ad99e17a19b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332967} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d1f277b-a634-584c-8716-a16b3efc218b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01a82786-6006-50b3-9639-081950d67e5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123474" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩$ and $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 5{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{4/3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨4\\cdot {0}^{4/3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{5\\cdot 0}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=2$ and ${c}_{2}=-2.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a159bc41-3073-54fd-9d41-96df91fdf37d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a159bc41-3073-54fd-9d41-96df91fdf37d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332972} :answer-field/id #uuid "334a7142-6723-5ba2-88dc-746ad9e1b227" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5527e6fb-25ea-5abb-bfe2-5caf5e77b00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}(e^4-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5527e6fb-25ea-5abb-bfe2-5caf5e77b00c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}(e^4-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332974} :answer-field/id #uuid "07ffd7dc-bcac-5d3f-b3d1-b57dffec5ed2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5a3b17e-dbd2-5a41-b6fd-4f7c093aad74" :question/math-academy-id "q-349120" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨4{t}^{2}-3t,\\,5{e}^{2t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨4{t}^{2}-3t,\\,5{e}^{2t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4{t}^{2}-3t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}5{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int (4{t}^{2}-3t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int 5{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t=5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}=\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨4{t}^{2}-3t,\\,5{e}^{2t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨(\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2},\\,(\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{2t}){|}_{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{4}{3}(8)-\\frac{3}{2}(4))-0,\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{32}{3}-6),\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{14}{3},\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{14}{3},\\,\\frac{5}{2}({e}^{4}-1)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71336adc-b8ab-570f-a41e-3a13bcbfe090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨27,\\,\\frac{14}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332977} {:answer/id #uuid "d22eff86-7b7b-5b44-aaa9-4d21282cef3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨22,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332978} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8de7be-6249-5fad-adb6-7ad8d727d789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨22,\\,\\frac{14}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332979} {:answer/id #uuid "72531e39-483e-508c-89cf-2761e1bdb608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨27,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332980} {:answer/id #uuid "15dca4c7-3011-5bf4-a411-9c51f5b2cd0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨25,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71336adc-b8ab-570f-a41e-3a13bcbfe090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨27,\\,\\frac{14}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332977} :answer-field/id #uuid "d018d7a9-e1d5-57f4-877e-e5a4c0f18fa7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fb6e671-f6b6-5a74-97b2-ded0b0f24246" :question/math-academy-id "q-50200" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}⟨4t-1,\\sqrt{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}⟨4t-1,\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{1}^{4}(4t-1)\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(2{t}^{2}-t){|}_{1}^{4},\\,(\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}){|}_{1}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(2(4)^{2}-4)-(2(1)^{2}-1),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,\\,\\frac{14}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e6ee661-ba22-542d-a9fb-b76d8076a27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\ln \\mid t \\mid, \\frac{1}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095702} {:answer/id #uuid "bb21cdf1-22bd-524b-852c-992658713584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095703} {:answer/id #uuid "c82b3f55-eede-588c-8f00-ece0e818fa7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- ⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid, \\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095704} {:answer/id #uuid "499e839a-bf75-5fd9-bdc6-858357101649" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\ln \\mid t \\mid,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095705} {:answer/id #uuid "57636129-14de-554a-a121-0e8f70645831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid, \\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb21cdf1-22bd-524b-852c-992658713584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095703} :answer-field/id #uuid "47c6edcd-4580-541c-8ae3-e21d3e20ddad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4a69144-d189-5ac0-bdfe-ac5dd5bddd37" :question/math-academy-id "q-50201" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨\\frac{3}{t},\\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{3}{t},\\,\\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{3}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{5}{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|,\\,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|,\\,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed9e6e31-6a91-5892-a70b-02e7ae6608b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332984} {:answer/id #uuid "6f4c9955-8e5b-5d36-b2b3-8f4811da3362" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}-5,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332985} {:answer/id #uuid "126a9654-7424-54a2-9fd3-163b468e3fa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}-5t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332986} {:answer/id #uuid "b1fc6e73-15d3-5f84-b825-7ef54859ad7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6t,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332987} {:answer/id #uuid "abf6850f-abd1-5e14-8783-9d909c4a9846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}-5t,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "126a9654-7424-54a2-9fd3-163b468e3fa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}-5t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332986} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a679aae-2dd8-50fb-82d2-22db7efec3ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4adae4a1-2b74-58fe-abb4-b356d959e36c" :question/math-academy-id "q-80462" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3{t}^{2}-5,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3{t}^{2}-5,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3{t}^{2}-5,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (3{t}^{2}-5)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}-5t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}-5t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3}-5t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b8e8a96-9973-5ffb-a692-45bf60b973a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332991} {:answer/id #uuid "14dd103f-69e8-5966-9e39-41a6ca90cf76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332992} {:answer/id #uuid "0edd8566-357e-5796-83ba-1da8b62e7650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332993} {:answer/id #uuid "267423a9-af09-5ebb-a456-596352097c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332994} {:answer/id #uuid "dca9ce97-ee20-5cbe-9fe4-8f2c57858563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14dd103f-69e8-5966-9e39-41a6ca90cf76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332992} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5a67a5-0e3d-5adc-88fa-817279c40f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed9275a1-ce69-572b-90c1-a522c36d6a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80463" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3496da0e-a912-529f-ac1c-bf604cdb59bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-1,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332998} {:answer/id #uuid "115bf5a7-c670-5b2a-a951-dde4b6ae211e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+1,\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332999} {:answer/id #uuid "26d7e3f5-c99a-55d7-92c7-e3edf3e59c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333000} {:answer/id #uuid "adbc70a9-661f-5ae3-8a95-309ed7e0fa25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333001} {:answer/id #uuid "d50cc422-cf84-53e7-af5e-1765870899df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-\\frac{1}{2},\\,2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26d7e3f5-c99a-55d7-92c7-e3edf3e59c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333000} :answer-field/id #uuid "c308601e-b0bf-5bb8-a2ae-a94cd63e565b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e8cce85e-bb38-5a8a-b3de-95c194a0eee1" :question/math-academy-id "q-85742" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,,{sec}^{2}⁡(t)⟩$ and $F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=⟨1,\\,0⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,,{sec}^{2}⁡(t)⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,,{sec}^{2}⁡(t)⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=⟨1,\\,0⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)-1⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14ed6fba-faef-52f5-9de1-b72e1bf595c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2{t}^{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333005} {:answer/id #uuid "7f19462c-73f1-57d1-bd17-22b7ac08ea5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333006} {:answer/id #uuid "7702b03f-f4ee-541d-9477-014f490715c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333007} {:answer/id #uuid "555f273d-0a0d-506b-9de1-4059a8c706bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333008} {:answer/id #uuid "6747640e-e7ce-5318-922e-18c6730da711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555f273d-0a0d-506b-9de1-4059a8c706bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333008} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ef240db-a443-5cce-9b62-c52f6a7c5849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e048aedd-212a-53bc-8a9e-1b74509a4df1" :question/math-academy-id "q-99263" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 1\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5f56ea7-9631-5f59-9187-61d953c00639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333012} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc97488-78fb-59c4-9546-6870aa183348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333013} {:answer/id #uuid "f598b8db-3592-5a75-8d76-a54d42c72eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333014} {:answer/id #uuid "9df959ad-243a-542d-8375-9dc3267642f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333015} {:answer/id #uuid "15e38a9f-18a5-55eb-b75c-399f1a7de01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨20,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fc97488-78fb-59c4-9546-6870aa183348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333013} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cbe63d8-b753-571d-a3a2-d74d931dde12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6a4c9ec-988e-50b9-a11d-a4ebe9c71ccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-99278" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{4}⟨2t-1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}⟨2t-1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨({t}^{2}-t)\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{4},\\,\\sqrt{t}\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{4}\\,\\,⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\text{ }({4}^{2}-4)-({1}^{2}-1),\\,\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f982d8-0849-5fd4-b739-36619914be95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8, 8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096266} {:answer/id #uuid "982b0851-09b6-5cad-a1b7-8128f84500ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096267} {:answer/id #uuid "b070c192-a544-52c8-aeb9-7bd0d500bc44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2, 8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096268} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f04580-f6b7-538d-ba56-29756fb2c80f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{6}, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096269} {:answer/id #uuid "65bdae85-8859-5781-b9c4-bf3e6b7ebffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{3}, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b070c192-a544-52c8-aeb9-7bd0d500bc44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2, 8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096268} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c5b54e-0ae8-5cc3-8312-664153890889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f8bf600-65ab-5cfd-b27b-b6c2905e2ce8" :question/math-academy-id "q-99361" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1}^{9}⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,1⟩\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{9}⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,1⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{1}^{9}1\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{t}\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{9},\\,t\\,\\,{|}_{1}^{9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{1},\\,9-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c45f96d-03b1-5bd6-bb3a-31d5d9f60d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{({e}^{2t}+e)}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333019} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b1a71d-f4b0-5165-94b6-4b0e922559d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333020} {:answer/id #uuid "166a60e6-716c-551b-a7dd-3beb0c13fae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333021} {:answer/id #uuid "bcefa098-1f2f-539a-970b-dabe8993220c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333022} {:answer/id #uuid "728197e8-77cf-5e4a-a9a8-bb0d0d95bf18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{2t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcefa098-1f2f-539a-970b-dabe8993220c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333022} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b09ba27-ddf7-5f44-89a9-f9023f3c7f27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb6f108b-b2c6-57c1-9132-69c2656eace2" :question/math-academy-id "q-99378" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 2{e}^{(2t+1)}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=2{e}^{(2t+1)},$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=2t+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 2{e}^{(2t+1)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 3{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{u}+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bee42e42-f04b-5290-b437-bfce84f79899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{3}^{t},\\,-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333026} {:answer/id #uuid "d55e86e8-b5aa-5e1a-84bd-7703bb7915ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333027} {:answer/id #uuid "7a773244-de03-5f03-aa3d-8a49dab4c5b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333028} {:answer/id #uuid "4de24f26-4285-5283-9ceb-9902cd759289" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2},\\,-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333029} {:answer/id #uuid "84ac24b3-f933-53cf-a0d6-ddd5c3822cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\\,-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d55e86e8-b5aa-5e1a-84bd-7703bb7915ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333027} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2cf6a5c-faf1-5be1-8a2d-4191bfe95f88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "056c0a76-101b-521d-8188-2f2f8cee2913" :question/math-academy-id "q-99392" :question/problem "$\\int ⟨{3}^{t},\\,{csc}^{2}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{3}^{t},\\,{csc}^{2}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {3}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
